Good morning,

We are instructed to notify a freeze and water damage loss for our client Harborline Cold Storage & Logistics, LLC. Our reference is TR/PROP/2025/4471.

Please note this loss is at the client's **Delaware terminal**, not the Baltimore cold store. It is the scheduled dry storage and cross-dock location at New Castle. The building is leased and the owner is Delaware River Industrial Trust, LP, who are the loss payee for that premises.

Broker reference: TR/PROP/2025/4471
Insured name: Harborline Cold Storage & Logistics, LLC
Date of loss: 1 February 2026
Loss location: 419 Delaware Terminal Road, New Castle, DE 19720
Risk location: Scheduled secondary premises - dry storage and cross-dock
Cause: Freeze - frozen sprinkler branch line
Estimated loss: USD 1,240,000

A sprinkler branch line in the unheated dock canopy froze and split during the
cold snap at the start of the month. It was found at 05:50 on Sunday and isolated
by 06:40, but there was standing water across about 31,000 sq ft of the
cross-dock floor by then.

Two 480V panels and an MCC took water and are not re-energised. Six dock leveller
pits were under. 214 of the 640 pallets on the floor had direct water contact and
137 of those are customer-owned, so there is a bailee element again.

A fire watch ran continuously from 07:00 on the 1st until the system was back in
service on the 4th, and the county was notified.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * emergency mitigation report
  * mitigation cost schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Mitigation is already at USD
407,130 and reconstruction has not started.

